I know that there are a lot of spoilers regarding pets and thieving,
but I don't think that any of them are particularily useful or
complete, and many are conflicting.

Things that I know:  (or think I know)

- A happy pet is a theiving pet.
- A well fed pet is a theiving pet.
- Pets become less likey to pick up and drop objects each time they
pick up and drop an object.

Good pet conditioning strategies include:
 - keeping a clean dungeon so your pet isn't picking up stuff.
 - saving tripe rations or other treats for shopping.
 - otherwise keeping pets well fed.
 - being nice to pets.
   - No displacing into traps or
   - hitting with missiles.

Good shop conditioning strategies include:
 - whipping darts down aisles to find mimics (just read that)
 - piling good stuff in a pile near the door and bad stuff with
   cursed objects. (helpful to be a priest, or just follow pet
   around)

Good shop robbing strategies include:
 - a magic whistle, oh yeah!
 - a leash can be helpful.
 - moving around to manouver shop keeper into right position
   and lead pet around.  (better with leash)

Once I discover that it isn't cursed, I generally pile all the
stuff I want opposite the door and as as close as possible in
the order of my preference.  I do as much of this as possible
with my pet outside the shop.  It is common to get a few items
easily and I want to pick them out.  Then I wait at the door,
or one step back if the corridor is leading outward and try
to manouver el petto once he picks something up.

In a food shop I don't put 10 food rations in a pile, I split
them up into 2's and 3's.

I've noticed that you cannot displace you pet in, or into, a
doorway.

